        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: যথেষ্ট",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যথেষ্ট — jôtheshṭô — \"enough; plenty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যথেষ্ট টাকা থাকলে আমরা নতুন বাড়ি কিনব। jôtheshṭô ṭākā thākle āmrā nôtun bāṛi kinbô. If we have enough money, we'll buy a new house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যথেষ্ট (jôtheshṭô) is Sanskrit yatheṣṭa, 'as much as one wishes' (Monier-Williams). Bengali turned it into plain 'enough'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
